     <h2>3. Recording of data on our website</h2>
     <p><strong>Cookies</strong></p>
     <p>In some instances, our website and its pages use so-called cookies. Cookies do not cause any damage to your computer and do not contain viruses. The purpose of cookies is to make our website more user friendly, effective and more secure. Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer and stored by your browser.</p>
+
+    <p><strong>Analytics (third party)</strong></p>
+    <p>We use a third-party analytics script only if you allow it. It is off by default, is never loaded on the sign-in and sign-up pages, and stays off if your browser sends a Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control signal. You can change your choice at any time via “Manage Privacy Preferences” in the footer.</p>
+
+    <p><strong>Accounts</strong></p>
+    <p>To create an account we collect only a username and a password. We do not ask for an email address or other personal details. Credentials are sent over HTTPS directly to our sign-in service and are not shared with analytics.</p>
+
+    <p><strong>Fonts and external resources</strong></p>
+    <p>Fonts are hosted on our own servers, so your IP address is not sent to a font provider. We limit referrer information sent to other sites and restrict which external hosts the site can contact.</p>
 </LegalLayout>
